From 8de75c111c7f8e0e8a9624c2c80eb2abe1a777ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:27:41 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: Add the qcom-ife pipeline handler and IPA

The CAMSS of Qualcomm Titan 17x (SC8280XP) processes Bayer frames in the
IFE pixel path: black level, lens shading, bad pixel and phase detection
pixel correction, Bayer denoising, demosaic, white balance, colour
correction, gamma and scaling, into NV12, with an AWB grid, focus
statistics and a Bayer histogram per frame. The kernel exposes it as
video nodes for the processed images and V4L2 extensible ISP parameter
and statistics nodes.

The pipeline handler drives a sensor through the CSIPHY and the CSID's
pixel path into one IFE, or into two for frames wider than one IFE line
(3840 pixels), splitting the frame at a column it chooses: one the lens
shading grid allows a stripe to start at, where the display output's
seam falls closest to a whole output column. It offers:

- a processed stream from the FULL output, and a second one from the
  display output (Viewfinder beside StillCapture), the larger of the two
  from FULL; the display output keeps the field of view of FULL;
- a RAW stream of the sensor frame from an RDI, in the largest mode,
  for phase detection in the HAL;
- requests that leave out the FULL or the RAW stream: each request's
  parameters name the outputs of its frame, and every buffer of a
  request takes the frame number of its parameters buffer, as
  V4L2VideoDevice renumbers each capture node from its first buffer;
- ScalerCrop applied to the display output per frame, reported as the
  window shown, sent only when it changes;
- restart of the streams after a device error, with the IPA's full
  parameters sent again.

The IPA implements, per frame on the statistics: AGC on the AWB grid
with the metering window of AfWindows, constraints on the Bayer
histogram of that window and flicker avoidance; AWB with the libipa
algorithms on the AWB grid means (grey world or Bayesian, by tuning
file) and the CCM interpolated by colour temperature; black level; gamma;
lens shading from the tuning data; bad pixel and phase detection pixel
correction; the adaptive Bayer filter's noise tables by gain; and the
FocusFoM of the focus statistics in the AfWindows region. It sets the
frame length from FrameDurationLimits. The sensor gets the exposure the
AGC computed from the latest statistics, not the one prepared when the
request was queued, so the AGC reacts within the sensor delays however
many requests are queued. The tuning files for the ov13b10
and the hi846 of the Huawei MateBook E Go come from its Windows camera
driver's tuning and calibration on the device.

The pipeline needs the kernel's IFE parameters and statistics nodes; the
statistics buffer layout, of ife17x-config.h, must match the kernel's.

Signed-off-by: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
